8a. TWO REAL BUGS FOUND WHILE WRITING THESE TESTS
-------------------------------------------------
Neither was on the checklist. Both were shipping.

  B1. `scan_screen.dart` OVERFLOWED ON A SHORT PHONE. The Scaffold body is a
      Column holding a fixed 300px camera preview; adding the error card pushed
      it 28px off a 360x720 screen. This fires on the single most common real
      failure -- a fresh install whose ML Kit model has not downloaded yet, so
      the "Waiting for a connection" card is exactly what the user sees.

      Fixed by reclaiming preview height (300 -> 160) only while an error card
      is up. The preview is not actionable during an error anyway.

      WRONG ALTERNATIVE, recorded so nobody retries it: wrapping the preview in
      `Flexible` is incorrect. It competes with the results list for the same
      free space and starves it -- that attempt turned 1 passing test into 14
      failures.

  B2. The Proceed button in `new_sale_screen.dart` sits at the bottom of a
      scrolling cart panel, so `tester.tap` on it silently missed. Two tests
      were failing for a reason that looked like "the dialog never opened".
      Not a shipping bug, but it was hiding whether completion worked at all.


